-- 2026-11-12 (later): the office rule OR27 was titled "Early Support Visits" with the same topics as the public answer K157.
-- An internal match that ties a public one makes the website chat hold its answer back, so "What are Early Support Visits?"
-- and "can someone come once a month" got "that is about how we run things on our end" (found by step 1449's live questions).
-- OR27 keeps its facts, with a title and topics only the office would ask for. Ask Cara in the Hub reads every internal rule's
-- question and answer, so the office still gets it. Only OR27 changes, and only when it still differs. K157 is untouched.
update public.kb_items set question = 'Exhibit J on the tablet', answer = 'Early Support Visits (office steps). A separate program, not a fourth care level. Springfield only. One 4-hour visit once a month ($152 a visit, $38 an hour) or every other week ($140 a visit, $35 an hour). No weekly option. One-time $99 assessment and setup, billed with the first visit; nothing is paid at the assessment. It is Exhibit J of the Client Care Agreement: on the tablet''s set-up screen tick the enrolling box, pick the schedule and type the regular visit day. Regular care is still 4-hour visits, 8 hours a week. Never promise the same caregiver or an extra visit. Steps are on Payors & Programs, Early Support Visits tab.', topics = array['exhibit j']::text[],
  alt_questions = array[]::text[], updated_at = now()
  where id = 'OR27' and audience = 'internal' and (question is distinct from 'Exhibit J on the tablet' or topics is distinct from array['exhibit j']::text[] or answer is distinct from 'Early Support Visits (office steps). A separate program, not a fourth care level. Springfield only. One 4-hour visit once a month ($152 a visit, $38 an hour) or every other week ($140 a visit, $35 an hour). No weekly option. One-time $99 assessment and setup, billed with the first visit; nothing is paid at the assessment. It is Exhibit J of the Client Care Agreement: on the tablet''s set-up screen tick the enrolling box, pick the schedule and type the regular visit day. Regular care is still 4-hour visits, 8 hours a week. Never promise the same caregiver or an extra visit. Steps are on Payors & Programs, Early Support Visits tab.');
